The three copies of sharpe.ts (backtest-check, deflated-sharpe-ratio-calculator,
minimum-track-record-length-calculator) contain `normInv`, an inverse of the standard normal
distribution. It follows CPython's implementation of Wichura's algorithm AS241 (PPND16), function
`_normal_dist_inv_cdf` of the statistics module: same branches and coefficients. Changes: translated from
Python to TypeScript, coefficients written in their shortest round-trip double form, and an input
outside (0, 1) throws a named error.

